WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.286 --> 00:00:07.777
Among the buildings in the dreary town of Mudfog was a workhouse, where the poor were housed and many of them were worked to death.

2
00:00:07.778 --> 00:00:14.212
Oliver Twist was born in this dismal place, but for a few minutes it was doubtful he would survive.

3
00:00:14.213 --> 00:00:25.932
At last he breathed, sneezed, and let out a loud wail. Hearing this, a young woman raised her head feebly from her pillow. "Let me see the child and die."

4
00:00:25.933 --> 00:00:31.024
"Oh, you must not talk about dying yet," said the doctor who had attended the birth.

5
00:00:31.025 --> 00:00:39.755
"Bless her heart, no," said the old pauper woman who was serving as nurse. "Think about being a mother to your new baby, dear."

6
00:00:39.756 --> 00:00:46.437
The young mother stretched out her hand toward the child. The doctor deposited the baby in her arms.

7
00:00:46.438 --> 00:00:52.523
She imprinted her cold lips passionately on his forehead, shuddered, and died.

8
00:00:52.524 --> 00:00:58.833
"It's all over," said the doctor. "She was a nice-looking girl. Where did she come from?"

9
00:00:58.834 --> 00:01:10.168
"She was brought here last night," replied the old woman. "She was found lying in the street. But where she came from or where she was going, nobody knows."

10
00:01:10.169 --> 00:01:22.902
The doctor leaned over the body. "The same old story." He shook his head. "No wedding ring. Well, good night. If the child cries, give it a little gruel."

11
00:01:22.903 --> 00:01:31.645
Wrapped in an old calico blanket, Oliver cried lustily. If he had known he was a workhouse orphan, he would have cried even louder.

12
00:01:31.646 --> 00:01:38.534
When Oliver was about eight months old, he was sent to a branch workhouse—a farm run by an elderly woman.

13
00:01:38.535 --> 00:01:42.383
Mrs. Mann was a woman of wisdom and experience.

14
00:01:42.384 --> 00:01:47.963
She knew what was good for the children under her care, and she knew what was good for her.

15
00:01:47.964 --> 00:01:54.540
So she took the greater part of their weekly stipends for her own use and fed the children as little as possible.

16
00:01:54.541 --> 00:02:00.531
By his tenth birthday, Oliver was a pale child, small for his age and quite thin.

17
00:02:00.532 --> 00:02:05.203
But luckily nature had planted a good, sturdy spirit in Oliver's heart.

18
00:02:05.204 --> 00:02:11.108
For he was spending his birthday locked in the coal cellar with two other orphans for daring to be hungry.

19
00:02:11.109 --> 00:02:16.938
Mrs. Mann looked out the window and saw a large, fat man fumbling with the latch on the front gate.

20
00:02:16.939 --> 00:02:26.263
"The parish officer is here!" she cried to her servant. "Take Oliver and those two brats upstairs and wash them right away before Mr. Bumble sees them!"

21
00:02:26.264 --> 00:02:36.991
"Why is this gate locked?" The man rattled the gate as Mrs. Mann appeared. "You're keeping a parish officer waiting. And I am here on official business!"

22
00:02:36.992 --> 00:02:46.254
"How delightful to see you, Mr. Bumble!" Mrs. Mann opened the gate. "I was just telling the dear children, who are so fond of you, that you're here."

23
00:02:46.255 --> 00:02:51.404
Mrs. Mann ushered him into the parlor, where he removed his hat, and they sat down.

24
00:02:51.405 --> 00:02:55.236
"Oliver Twist is ten years old today," said Mr. Bumble.

25
00:02:55.237 --> 00:02:58.236
"Bless him," interrupted Mrs. Mann.

26
00:02:58.237 --> 00:03:07.238
"And despite offering a reward of ten pounds—later increased to twenty pounds—the parish has never been able to discover the names of his parents."

27
00:03:07.239 --> 00:03:09.555
"Then how did he get a name?"

28
00:03:09.556 --> 00:03:24.725
Mr. Bumble drew himself up with pride. "I name all the orphans in alphabetical order. The last was Swubble, then Twist, then Unwin. But returning to business, Oliver is too old to remain here. I've

29
00:03:24.726 --> 00:03:29.540
come myself to take him back to the workhouse, so let me see him at once." Mrs.

30
00:03:29.541 --> 00:03:31.963
Mann went to fetch Oliver. "Make

31
00:03:31.964 --> 00:03:35.889
a bow to the gentleman, Oliver," she said when they returned. Oliver

32
00:03:35.890 --> 00:03:37.461
bowed. "Very

33
00:03:37.462 --> 00:03:47.051
good, Oliver. Now come along with me." And with that, Mr. Bumble put on his hat and bade the surprised Mrs. Mann good day. Mr.

34
00:03:47.052 --> 00:03:51.862
Bumble walked quickly down the road with little Oliver clutching his coat cuff. "Are

35
00:03:51.863 --> 00:03:55.680
we nearly there?" Oliver gasped every quarter mile. "Not

36
00:03:55.681 --> 00:03:59.600
yet," Mr. Bumble said with growing impatience. At

37
00:03:59.601 --> 00:04:03.466
last they arrived at a huge, prison-like building. "You've

38
00:04:03.467 --> 00:04:07.923
come here to be taught a useful trade," said Mr. Bumble. "Starting

39
00:04:07.924 --> 00:04:13.691
tomorrow morning at six o'clock, you'll pick apart old ropes so they can be reused." Oliver

40
00:04:13.691 --> 00:04:19.242
barely had time to look around before he was hurried away to receive his dreary uniform. That

41
00:04:19.243 --> 00:04:24.580
night he sobbed himself to sleep on a hard bed in a room full of other boys. Three

42
00:04:24.581 --> 00:04:32.423
months passed. The board running the workhouse decided that too many poor people were taking advantage of its services. To

43
00:04:32.424 --> 00:04:37.245
reduce the number of paupers, they drastically reduced the amount of food. Now

44
00:04:37.246 --> 00:04:44.308
each boy was allowed only one small bowl of gruel. The boys were fed in a great stone hall. Once

45
00:04:44.309 --> 00:04:51.140
a day, the master of the workhouse, assisted by two women, ladled out the gruel from a large copper pot. "If

46
00:04:51.141 --> 00:04:57.124
I don't get more to eat," said a new boy, "I might have to eat one of you." He

47
00:04:57.125 --> 00:05:01.978
glared at the other boys with a wild, hungry look in his eyes, frightening them. That

48
00:05:01.979 --> 00:05:10.208
night the boys decided that someone had to ask the master for more food. They drew lots, and Oliver got the job. The

49
00:05:10.209 --> 00:05:17.201
next evening the boys arrived in the dining hall. They stood in line while the master filled their bowls. Then

50
00:05:17.202 --> 00:05:24.295
they sat down, and the gruel quickly disappeared. The boys whispered to each other and winked at Oliver. Oliver

51
00:05:24.296 --> 00:05:31.367
was desperate with hunger and reckless with misery. He rose from the table and walked toward the master. "Please,

52
00:05:31.368 --> 00:05:36.365
sir." Oliver held up his bowl. "I want some more." The

53
00:05:36.366 --> 00:05:42.020
master aimed a blow at Oliver's head with his ladle. "Call Mr. Bumble!" The

54
00:05:42.021 --> 00:05:49.257
parish officer came running from a board meeting, and when he heard Oliver's request, he ran right back. "I

55
00:05:49.258 --> 00:05:56.518
beg your pardon, Mr. Limbkins," Mr. Bumble said to the head of the board. "Oliver Twist has asked for more food." There

56
00:05:56.519 --> 00:05:59.506
was horror on every face in the room. "For

57
00:05:59.507 --> 00:06:11.340
more ?" said Mr. Limbkins. "Compose yourself, Bumble, and answer me. Do I understand he asked for more after he'd eaten the amount allotted to him?"

58
00:06:11.341 --> 00:06:14.157
"He did, sir," replied Mr. Bumble.

59
00:06:14.158 --> 00:06:20.832
"That boy will come to a bad end." Mr. Limbkins shook his head, and no one disagreed.

60
00:06:20.833 --> 00:06:30.571
Oliver was instantly locked up. The next morning a notice was posted on the workhouse gate, offering five pounds to anyone who wanted an apprentice.

61
00:06:30.572 --> 00:06:39.526
In other words, they were looking for anyone who would take Oliver Twist off the hands of the parish.

